# Harmonic conjugates of bisector feet — the feet of the internal and external bisectors from A divide BC in the same ratio (source: Coxeter & Greitzer, Geometry Revisited)
A B C = triangle
X = meet(bisector(B, A, C), line(B, C))
Y = meet(perp_line(A, bisector(B, A, C)), line(B, C))
prove eqratio(X, B, X, C, Y, B, Y, C)
